# The strict flag definition -- the vet-side contract.
#
# This file is a SCHEMA DOCUMENT for `aontu vet` only; base.aon never
# includes it.  Three language limits force the split (README, "Gaps"):
#   - a constraint meeting a ranked default in a conjunct does not
#     resolve, so the catalog cannot carry these types inline on the
#     defaulted fields;
#   - the disjunct form (***false | boolean) silently loses rank
#     arbitration through the effective-view references;
#   - a hide()-marked vet anchor silently disables the incompleteness
#     verdict, so these defs stay unhidden -- which is also why this
#     file cannot be part of the generated model.
#
# Used as:
#   aontu vet --at '$.Flag' --closed flag-schema.aon <candidate.json>
#   aontu vet --at '$.Flag'          flag-schema.aon <one-resolved-flag.json>
#
# A whole effective view is validated flag-by-flag: a spread anchor
# whose template REFERENCES $.Flag does not resolve under --at, which
# re-roots the document at the anchor (README, "Gaps").  So the check
# extracts each resolved flag with `get` and vets it against $.Flag.

# THE FIELD SHAPES, NAMED. `%name:` at the top level declares an
# alias; `%name` in value position uses it. An alias does not generate
# and does not appear in canon, so this file and the one with every
# constraint written out are the same document with the same `aon1-`
# hash -- a name for a value, and nothing else.
#
# `flags.aon` repeats these four shapes and does NOT name them, for two
# reasons. An alias reaches nothing outside the document it is declared
# in -- there is no construct for carrying a name across a file
# boundary deliberately -- so it would have to be a second declaration
# rather than a shared one. And `flags.aon` writes them inside a SPREAD
# TEMPLATE, where an alias reference is not resolved and leaks into
# canon as `$.%Date`, changing the document's `aon1-` hash: BUGS.md 73.
# Here there is no spread, so the names cost nothing.
%Key: string & re("^[a-z][a-z0-9_.\\-]*$") & length(min(3)) & length(max(64))
%Owner: string & re("^[a-z0-9._\\-]+@acme\\.example$")
%Description: string & length(min(12)) & length(max(160))
%Date: string & re("^\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}$")

Flag: key: %Key
Flag: flag_type: "boolean" | "percentage" | "variant"
Flag: owner: %Owner
Flag: description: %Description
Flag: created: %Date
Flag: expiry: %Date
Flag: enabled: boolean
Flag: rollout: integer & min(0) & max(100)
Flag: variant?: string & re("^[a-z][a-z0-9\\-]*$")
Flag: message?: string & length(max(80))
